          "filename": "2018-06-07 Sycamore Gap Tree (Acer pseudoplatanus), next to Hadrian’s Wall UK.jpg",
          "caption": "The Sycamore Gap Tree or “Robin Hood Tree” is a sycamore tree (Acer pseudoplatanus) standing next to Hadrian's Wall near Haltwhistle, Northumberland, England. Crag Lough and the villages of Once Brewed and Haltwhistle are nearby. Image taken on June 7, 2018. \nFollow-up Note: This 200-year-old tree was cut down in an act of vandalism on the night of September 28, 2023.",
